  "caption": "Quinn's first surf trip: five sessions a day, noodle arms by day two and a grumpy lower back by day three.\n\nMost of surfing is paddling, lying arched with the shoulders working overhead. Surf trips and big swells can suddenly multiply that load, which is when shoulder, back and neck aches often flare.\n\nWhat can help: train the rotator cuff, shoulder blades and rows on land about twice a week, keep the upper back and hips moving, build fitness before a trip, and warm up before paddling out.\n\nShoulder or back pain that doesn't settle with less surfing is worth getting checked. Any head or neck injury in the water needs immediate medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
